* TTY echo — echo typewriter input back until a line starting with "."
* Adapted from Knuth TAOCP / jflude/taocp examples
*
* Device 19 (typewriter): 14 words = 70 chars per block.
* The program reads one block at a time, prints it, and repeats.
* It halts when the first character of a block is "." (MIX byte 40).
*
* Usage:
*   1. Open the TTY tab in the I/O panel.
*   2. Type text in the TTY Input box (70 chars per "card").
*      End your input with a line whose first character is "."
*      e.g.:  "HELLO WORLD                                                           ."
*   3. Assemble & Load, then Run.

TTY     EQU     19
BUF     EQU     200
        ORIG    1000
OUTPUT  OUT     BUF(TTY)      * print BUF to typewriter
START   IN      BUF(TTY)      * read 14 words (70 chars) from TTY input
        JBUS    *(TTY)        * wait if busy (NOP: always ready)
        LDA     BUF           * load first word (first 5 chars of block)
        CMPA    PERIOD(1:1)   * compare byte 1 (first char) with "."
        JNE     OUTPUT        * not a period line → print it and read next
        HLT
PERIOD  ALF     "."           * "." = MIX byte 40
        END     START
